From: Tiaoge-tou <85100527+Tiaoge-tou@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:46:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS front end: close DmRateLink's tick method (a brace lost
 in the 120 Hz port)

Patch 0077's DmRateLink -tick: never closed its body before @end, so front_ios.m does not parse (the shell build's xcodebuild stopped at the @end line, front_ios.m:124). The one-game CI jobs that compile the iOS sources are path-filtered and the ported queue was only ever check-applied, so the first real compile is the fork's shell build (run 41703116512). One line: the missing closing brace. A brace scan of every iOS source finds no other imbalance.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Fix a syntax error the 0077 port introduced: DmRateLink's tick method in front_ios.m was missing its closing brace, so the file does not compile; found by the first real iOS compile, the fork's shell build.
Issue: Tiaoge-tou/NX2Apple PROJECT.md Phase 4

---
 dm/ios/Sources/front_ios.m | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dm/ios/Sources/front_ios.m b/dm/ios/Sources/front_ios.m
index 16e2f9f..0ef51e2 100644
--- a/dm/ios/Sources/front_ios.m
+++ b/dm/ios/Sources/front_ios.m
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@ static DmRateLink *g_rate_link;
     if (++self.ticks < 30) return;   // the rate must hold for 30 display frames before the host follows it, either way
     self.cur = hz; self.ticks = 0;
     dm_display_set_hz(hz);
+}
 @end
 
 // Hades II's HUD lays out against the size its script computes in RunLogic.lua (UpdateConfigOptionCache), which reads the engine's
